// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildSpecMarkdown > renders a deterministic, self-consistent spec 1`] = `
"# Design spec: \`player.ext.critdmg\`

**Status:** proposed
**Type:** \`float\`
**Used by:** extstats / compact / critdmg_label (label)
**Update frequency:** on stat recalculation

## Definition

Extended crit-damage percentage shown in the stats panel.

This variable is referenced by a \`ui_panels\` layout binding but is not yet exposed by the hybrasyl server. Until it ships, Brigid treats the binding as unbound and the control renders static (see docs/ui-panel-layout-format.md).

## Server delivery

How a new value reaches the client is decided by the document repo's \`docs/plans/brigid/BRIG-53-attributes-replacement-contract.md\` (status: proposed). It replaces retail 0x08 with \`0x0008\` Attributes inside the negotiated extension dialect. Two routes follow from it.

### Route A — an ExtendedStats id

For a numeric value about the player. Add a member to the stat enum in \`Hybrasyl.Protocol\`, with an explicit \`= N\`: an id is permanent once it ships. The server sends it in the \`0x0008\` ExtendedStats block as \`[u16 statId][f64 value]\`. A new stat needs no dialect version bump. Who owns the id registry is still open (HS-1239).

### Route B — a new opcode

For a value with its own cadence or shape, or one that is not a number. Allocate the opcode in \`Hybrasyl.Protocol\`'s \`docs/ALLOCATIONS.md\` first; the packet class lives in DALib.

**Recommended:** Route B — a new opcode

## Wire format

- Payload: \`f64\`, the value of an ExtendedStats record (route A); or a field of the new packet (route B).

## Client / Brigid expectations

- \`WorldState\` gains a \`float\` property that mirrors \`player.ext.critdmg\`, updated when the packet arrives.
- Raise the matching \`Changed\` event on update so bound controls refresh.
- On the layout side, a bound \`label\`/\`progressbar\` renders the numeric value (with optional \`format\`).

## Binding usage

\`\`\`xml
<label name="my_label" rect="0,0,80,14" bind="player.ext.critdmg" format="{value:0.0}"/>
\`\`\`
"
`;
